            <ArticleTitle>Fever as an adverse reaction to carbamazepine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>520-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two middle-aged women developed fever and abnormal liver function tests while taking carbamazepine. In one case the fever recurred following drug challenge. There are possible links to the known immune-related effects of the drug. Carbamazepine should be considered as a cause if fever or cholestasis develops in any person taking the drug.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
